+### Sharing
+
+A list has its owner and members, each member being an `editor` or a `viewer`. Every list answered by the API carries
+the caller's `role`: `owner`, `editor` or `viewer`.
+
+| | owner | editor | viewer |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| read the list, its tasks, tags, comments, activity and members | yes | yes | yes |
+| create, change and delete tasks; comment | yes | yes | no |
+| rename or delete the list; invite, revoke, remove members | yes | no | no |
+
+Someone who is not on the list gets 404 everywhere. A member who lacks the right for a request gets
+`403 { "error": "you do not have the right to do this" }`.
+
+| Method and path | Body | Answers |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /api/lists/:id/invitations` | `{ "role": "viewer" \| "editor", "expires_in_hours"? }` | 201 `{ "id", "token", "url", "role", "expires_at" }`; owner only. `expires_in_hours` is above 0 and at most 720, 72 by default |
+| `GET /api/lists/:id/invitations` | | 200, `[{ "id", "role", "created_at", "expires_at" }]`: the pending ones (not accepted, not expired); owner only |
+| `DELETE /api/lists/:id/invitations/:invitationId` | | 204: the link stops working; 404 if it is not pending; owner only |
+| `POST /api/invitations/:token/accept` | | 200, the list, with the caller's new `role`; 404 for an unknown or revoked token, 410 if it expired or was used |
+| `GET /api/lists/:id/members` | | 200, `[{ "id", "username", "role" }]`, the owner first, then by name |
+| `DELETE /api/lists/:id/members/:userId` | | 204; owner only; 400 for the owner, 404 for someone who is not a member |
+
+Notes:
+
+- `url` is `<base>/invite/<token>`, where `<base>` is `BASE_URL` if set, else the host of the request. Opening it
+  serves the page, which keeps the token, asks to sign in or create an account if needed, accepts the invitation
+  and shows the list. The page answers it with `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`.
+- The token is shown once, when the invitation is created: only its hash is stored. To send a link again, create
+  another one.
+- An invitation works once. A person who is already a member keeps the better of their current role and the
+  invitation's; the owner accepting their own invitation changes nothing.
+- Removing a member ends their access at once. The tasks assigned to them become unassigned and their planned
+  reminders are cancelled.
+- A task can be assigned to the owner or any member of its list, and to nobody else (400).
+- Reminders and digests go to the assignee of a task only while they can still see its list.
+
